cmd-wg_stasis-desc = Shows which grids are in stasis, and wakes, pins or unpins one.
cmd-wg_stasis-help = Usage: wg_stasis | wg_stasis wake <netEntity> | wg_stasis pin <netEntity> | wg_stasis unpin <netEntity>. With no arguments it counts grids by state and lists the largest ones in stasis. A grid pinned here stays awake until unpinned.
cmd-wg_stasis-hint = wake, pin or unpin
cmd-wg_stasis-usage = Usage: wg_stasis [wake|pin|unpin <netEntity>]
cmd-wg_stasis-no-grid = {$grid} is not a grid.
cmd-wg_stasis-states = Grids: {$awake} awake, {$pausing} going into stasis, {$paused} in stasis, {$waking} waking, {$excluded} never; {$pinned} pinned.
cmd-wg_stasis-largest = Largest grids in stasis, by paused entities:
cmd-wg_stasis-woken = Woke {$grid}; it stays awake for at least 60 s.
cmd-wg_stasis-held = {$grid} was not in stasis; it stays awake for at least 60 s.
cmd-wg_stasis-disabled = Grid stasis is off (wg.stasis.enabled); nothing was done.
cmd-wg_stasis-pinned = Pinned {$grid} awake.
cmd-wg_stasis-not-pinned = {$grid} has no admin pin; nothing was done.
cmd-wg_stasis-unpinned = Unpinned {$grid}; it can go into stasis again.
cmd-wg_stasis-unpinned-held = Took the admin pin off {$grid}, but other pins still keep it awake.
cmd-wg_stasis-pressure = Entity pressure {$pressure} of 1; a grid goes into stasis after {$idle} s unattended.

cmd-wg_coldstore-desc = Lists stored wrecks, and stores or restores one.
cmd-wg_coldstore-help = Usage: wg_coldstore | wg_coldstore store <grid netEntity> | wg_coldstore restore <stand-in netEntity | all>. With no arguments it lists stored grids: stand-in, entities, bytes, age and state. Store skips only the time in stasis and says why a grid can't be stored.
cmd-wg_coldstore-hint = store or restore
cmd-wg_coldstore-usage = Usage: wg_coldstore [store <grid> | restore <stand-in|all>]
cmd-wg_coldstore-no-entity = {$entity} is not an entity.
cmd-wg_coldstore-storing = Storing {$entity}.
cmd-wg_coldstore-refused = Can't store {$entity}: {$reason}
cmd-wg_coldstore-not-stored = {$entity} is not a stored grid's stand-in.
cmd-wg_coldstore-restored = Restored {$entity}.
cmd-wg_coldstore-restore-failed = Could not restore {$entity}; its stand-in and bytes are kept. See the server log.
cmd-wg_coldstore-restore-no-bytes = Could not restore {$entity}: its bytes are missing. Its stand-in is kept. See the server log.
cmd-wg_coldstore-queued-all = Queued {$count} grids to restore, one a tick. Grids that failed too often get one more try.
cmd-wg_coldstore-summary = Stored: {$grids} grids, {$entities} entities, {$bytes} bytes. This round: {$stores} stored, {$restores} restored, {$aborts} aborted, {$failures} failed loads, {$expired} expired.
cmd-wg_coldstore-state-stored = stored
cmd-wg_coldstore-state-failed = failed {$tries}x ({$error})

wg-coldstore-why-disabled = cold storage or grid stasis is off (wg.coldstore.enabled, wg.stasis.enabled).
wg-coldstore-why-aborted = storing it failed once this round.
wg-coldstore-why-not-grid = it is not a grid.
wg-coldstore-why-busy = another grid is being stored.
wg-coldstore-why-policy = only ownerless grids in open space are stored, and owned ships with wg.coldstore.player_ships on.
wg-coldstore-why-jobs = its station has open job slots.
wg-coldstore-why-not-idle = it has not been in stasis long enough.
wg-coldstore-why-pinned = something is holding it awake.
wg-coldstore-why-map = its map is paused or gone.
wg-coldstore-why-docked = it is docked.
wg-coldstore-why-moving = it is drifting or spinning.
wg-coldstore-why-watched = someone is within restore range.
wg-coldstore-why-near-grid = another grid is near.
wg-coldstore-why-worldgen = it is worldgen debris.
wg-coldstore-why-contract = a contract uses it.
wg-coldstore-why-claim = a claim, deed or squatter points at it.
wg-coldstore-why-rule = a game rule or admin event holds it.
wg-coldstore-why-corruption = corruption grows on it.
wg-coldstore-why-npc = a ship is docking with or following it.
wg-coldstore-why-minded = something aboard has a mind or a player.
wg-coldstore-why-unsaved = something aboard can't be saved, such as a mob.
wg-coldstore-why-small = it has too few entities to be worth it.

cmd-wg_planetstore-desc = Lists worlds and what the planet store has done with them, and unloads or loads one.
cmd-wg_planetstore-help = Usage: wg_planetstore | wg_planetstore unload <surface id> | wg_planetstore load <surface id>. With no arguments it lists every world: state, entities stored and kept, bytes, how long it has been empty and who is keeping it loaded. Unload ignores who is there; with wg.planetstore.enabled off, or someone there, the world comes straight back.
cmd-wg_planetstore-hint = unload or load
cmd-wg_planetstore-usage = Usage: wg_planetstore [unload <surface id> | load <surface id>]
cmd-wg_planetstore-no-world = {$world} is not a world's surface id.
cmd-wg_planetstore-unloading = Unloading {$world}.
cmd-wg_planetstore-loading = Loading {$world}.
cmd-wg_planetstore-refused = Can't unload {$world}: {$reason}
cmd-wg_planetstore-summary = {$entities} entities are out of the world in unloaded planets.
cmd-wg_planetstore-row = {$world}: {$state}, {$stored} stored, {$kept} kept asleep, {$bytes} bytes, empty {$empty} s, kept loaded by: {$who}. {$error}
cmd-wg_planetstore-nobody = nobody
wg-planetstore-why-not-planet = it is not a planet.
wg-planetstore-why-busy = another world is being unloaded.
wg-planetstore-why-not-loaded = it is not loaded.
wg-planetstore-why-arriving = a hull is hopping in
wg-planetstore-why-player = a player is there
wg-planetstore-why-watching = a player is watching it
wg-planetstore-why-mind = a body with a mind is there
wg-planetstore-why-jobs = a station there has jobs open
wg-planetstore-why-contract = a contract points into it
